"Marc Schlensog" <mschlens+news@gmail.com> wrote in message 
news:20110913075512.2482ade7@jones.schlensman.homeunix.net...
> Hi folks,
>
> I am planning to add a second CPU to my (finally working) DS20E. Is
> there anything to look out for except, of course, choosing CPU boards
> of the same speed or is it safe to assume that CPU boards of the same
> speed are similar enough to be able to run happily in one box?
>
> More precisely, the box currently has a 667MHz module in it with the
> PN 54-30060-03 and I'm looking at a module with the PN 54-30060-01.
>
> Thanks,
>
> Marc

You folks are lucky that I keep this crap around...  Found this in an old 
configuration guide.  Yes the -01 and -03 work together.  And for multi-cpu 
systems, CPU 0 is where the SROM and SRM are loaded from.  I don't think the 
system cares about the stuff on the other CPU cards so if you start moving 
cards between slots, you might see older versions appear.  I don't think the 
SRM update code knows how to update SROM/SRM on another other than 0.

I don't have anything on the subtle differences between the variants (BA, 
BB, BC, BD) and the passes (2.2.3 and 2.6).

John


Variants
Intermixing the KN310-AA (DS20) CPU and the KN310-BA (DS20E) CPU.

The -AA or -BA variants of the KN310 cannot be used to determine processor 
compatibility. The actual part number must be used.

DS20 processors with numbers are 54-24758-03 & -05, will work together; they 
have the same EV chips in them (No longer orderable).
DS20 and DS20E processors 54-24758-33 & -35 will work together, as they have 
the same EV chips in them. These cannot be mixed with -03 and -05 (DS20) 
or -43 and -45 (DS20 or DS20E).

DS20 and DS20E processors 54-24758-43 & -45 will work together; they have 
the same EV chips in them. These cannot be mixed with -03 and -05 (DS20) 
or -33 and -35 (DS20 or DS20E).

DS20E processors 54-30060 -01, -02, -03, -04 can be mixed together.

System               Model Number            CPU            Description
DS20E                54-24758-33               KN310-BA   500 MHz CPU, EV6 
4MB Motorola/IBM Pass 2.5
                         54-24758-35

DS20E                54-24758-43              KN310-CA    500 MHz CPU, EV67 
4MB IBM Pass 2.5
                         54-24758-45

DS20E                54-30060-01              KN311-BA,BB,BC,BD 667MHz CPU, 
EV67 8MB IBM/Sony Cache Pass 2.2.3
                         54-30060-02

DS20E                54-30060-03              KN311-CA,CB,CC,CD 667MHz CPU, 
EV67 8MB IBM/Sony Cache Pass 2.6
                         54-30060-04

DS20E                54-30482-02              KN312-BB,BC,BD  833MHz CPU, 
EV68 8MB IBM/Sony Cache




