> > I am planning to add a second CPU to my (finally working) DS20E. Is
> > there anything to look out for except, of course, choosing CPU boards
> > of the same speed or is it safe to assume that CPU boards of the same
> > speed are similar enough to be able to run happily in one box?
>
> > More precisely, the box currently has a 667MHz module in it with the
> > PN 54-30060-03 and I'm looking at a module with the PN 54-30060-01.
>
> > Thanks,
>
> > Marc
>
> Not sure if it was what we started out with, but in order to activate
> the second CPU we needed to buy an SMP licence. Now that was back when
> Compaq was running things so maybe things changed (or maybe not)
>
> Neil Rieck
> Kitchener / Waterloo / Cambridge,
> Ontario, Canada.http://www3.sympatico.ca/n.rieck/OpenVMS.html

Neil,
there used to be an SMP license (and kit) before VMS V5.0 arrived.
Multiprocessor, actually
just dual processor, support was built in and activated or liberated
by applying the kit.
IIRC it did not install new system images but rather patched existing
ones. It was expensive.
We ran a couple of VAX 8350's under VMS V4.7 and the order did not
include the SMP licenses.
Given their pricetag we decided to wait 4 months and install V5
instead.
Today with LMF and PAK's all you need is a OPENVMS-ALPHA license with
sufficient units
to support the second processor. In a hobbyist situation it does not
matter since all Montagar
supplied licenses have UNITS set to 0 which translates to infinite so
will always load and work.
Hans


