You might want to set the firmware at the same levels should they
differ.
I'm fairly new to the DS20E, was given a dual cpu 667MHz system just
two months ago.
However I have added cpu's to AlphaServer 1200 systems and all there
is to do is open the
box, remove one memory board (that applies to the AS1200, not the
DS20(E)) plug in the
second cpu and reseat that memory board.

Two notes/anecdotes:
- the AS1200 has a white box variant that runs Windows only. You can
mix DS5305 and AS1200
processors though the system always identifies itself as an AS1200.
- your VMS license requirements will change. If you're running a
Montagar license that has 0 points,
no problem. No effect on layered product PAK requirements.
Hans


