I suspect the official answer is the parts must be the same revision
too, which probably really means "compatible revisions" but it's too
hard to keep details of what's compatible. As pointed out above, the
two parts you have are not the same revision.

You've got the parts, so you might as well try it (what harm can it
do... think about that).

You might also want to think about the possible consequences of
occasional unexpected behaviour if there were, for example, some
oddness that only showed up occasionally when mixing different
revisions. These things have happened in the past, albeit
infrequently, and SMP systems are good candidates for revealing
oddness.

Don't forget you may need to update firmware too.

Have a lot of fun
John


